WEBVTT

00:41.250 --> 00:42.251
It's time to go.

00:44.670 --> 00:45.671
Did you hear me?

00:46.964 --> 00:48.758
This is an evacuation. You understand?

00:50.343 --> 00:51.469
You have to come with me.

00:52.261 --> 00:53.262
Why?

00:54.096 --> 00:55.890
Because they told me,
so now I'm telling you.

00:57.225 --> 00:58.851
Everyone in this village, everyone.

00:59.852 --> 01:01.646
It's not safe here.
There's radiation in the air.

01:01.729 --> 01:02.730
What's wrong with you?

01:03.814 --> 01:05.191
Do you know how old I am?

01:07.026 --> 01:09.070
I don't know. Old.

01:10.154 --> 01:11.155
I'm 82.

01:12.365 --> 01:13.991
I've lived here my whole life.

01:14.700 --> 01:17.578
Right here, that house, this place.

01:18.537 --> 01:20.456
What do I care about safe?

01:22.291 --> 01:23.334
I have a job.

01:24.126 --> 01:25.127
Don't cause trouble.

01:25.962 --> 01:26.963
Trouble?

01:28.297 --> 01:31.133
You're not the first soldier
to stand here with a gun.

01:32.218 --> 01:34.595
When I was 12, the revolution came.

01:35.471 --> 01:38.099
Czar's men. Then Bolsheviks.

01:38.891 --> 01:41.060
Boys like you marching in lines.

01:41.769 --> 01:43.938
They told us to leave. No.

01:45.022 --> 01:47.108
Then there was Stalin and his famine,

01:47.775 --> 01:48.901
the Holodomor.

01:49.944 --> 01:53.155
My parents died.
Two of my sisters died.

01:54.031 --> 01:55.950
They told the rest of us to leave.

01:56.784 --> 01:57.785
No.

01:58.411 --> 01:59.870
Then the Great War.

02:00.746 --> 02:02.873
German boys. Russian boys.

02:03.666 --> 02:06.877
More soldiers,
more famine, more bodies.

02:08.337 --> 02:10.006
My brothers never came home.

02:11.215 --> 02:13.426
But I stayed, and I'm still here.

02:14.510 --> 02:16.429
After all that I have seen,

02:18.055 --> 02:19.598
so I should leave now,

02:20.016 --> 02:22.393
because of something
I cannot see at all?

02:23.519 --> 02:24.520
No.

02:40.328 --> 02:41.329
Just one moment!

02:51.339 --> 02:52.340
It's time to go.

02:59.388 --> 03:01.140
Please stand up now.

03:12.318 --> 03:13.486
This is your last warning.

03:30.711 --> 03:31.754
It's time to go.

04:45.995 --> 04:46.996
Come on.

05:51.268 --> 05:52.269
Point four.

06:04.198 --> 06:05.199
Point six.

06:11.330 --> 06:12.331
Fifteen.

07:10.180 --> 07:11.223
Legasov.

07:13.851 --> 07:14.852
I'll meet him there.

08:14.161 --> 08:15.913
The atom
is a humbling thing.

08:18.415 --> 08:20.292
It's not humbling, it's humiliating.

08:22.503 --> 08:24.129
Why is the core still exposed
to the air?

08:24.213 --> 08:25.798
Why have we not already covered it up?

08:26.382 --> 08:29.718
We want to,
but we can't get close enough.

08:30.469 --> 08:33.681
The debris on the roof is graphite
from the core itself.

08:34.431 --> 08:37.976
Until we can push it off the roof
back into the reactor,

08:38.352 --> 08:40.312
it'll kill anyone who gets near it.

08:41.480 --> 08:44.775
You can see
the roof is in three levels.

08:45.192 --> 08:47.736
We've named them.
The small one here is Katya.

08:48.320 --> 08:50.280
1,000 roentgen per hour.

08:50.698 --> 08:53.367
Presume two hours of exposure
is fatal.

08:53.575 --> 08:55.119
The one on the side, Nina.

08:55.369 --> 08:57.538
2,000 roentgen. One hour, fatal.

08:57.621 --> 09:00.666
We used remote-control bulldozers
in Afghanistan.

09:00.749 --> 09:03.043
Too heavy. They'd fall right through.

09:04.044 --> 09:05.045
So then...

09:05.629 --> 09:06.797
Moon rovers.

09:07.673 --> 09:09.675
Lunokhod STR-1 's. They're light.

09:09.758 --> 09:12.428
And if we line them with lead,
they can withstand the radiation.

09:12.720 --> 09:14.179
We couldn't put a man on the moon.

09:14.888 --> 09:16.974
At least we can keep a man off a roof.

09:17.307 --> 09:19.476
That is the most
important thing, General.

09:19.560 --> 09:22.396
Under no circumstances
can men go up there.

09:23.021 --> 09:24.314
Robots only.

09:25.357 --> 09:27.109
What about this large section here?

09:28.736 --> 09:29.737
Masha.

09:31.238 --> 09:32.740
12,000 roentgen.

09:34.825 --> 09:36.827
If you were to stand there
in full protective gear

09:36.910 --> 09:38.662
head-to-toe for two minutes,

09:38.746 --> 09:40.539
your life expectancy
would be cut in half.

09:40.622 --> 09:42.750
By three minutes,
you're dead within months.

09:43.208 --> 09:45.919
Even our lunar rovers
won't work on Masha.

09:46.253 --> 09:49.214
That amount of gamma radiation
penetrates everything.

09:49.631 --> 09:53.135
The particles literally shred
the circuits in microchips apart.

09:53.385 --> 09:55.512
If it's more complicated
than a light switch,

09:55.929 --> 09:57.306
Masha will destroy it.

09:57.598 --> 09:58.974
It would be fair to say that

09:59.057 --> 10:01.769
that piece of roof
is the most dangerous place on Earth.

10:08.358 --> 10:10.903
So, what do we do?

10:14.156 --> 10:15.866
That's what we wanted to ask you.

12:33.587 --> 12:35.172
Tent 181?

12:50.103 --> 12:51.521
It's all right. It's free.

12:52.814 --> 12:53.941
It's a little early.

13:07.579 --> 13:08.580
Bacho.

13:10.958 --> 13:11.959
Pavel.

13:13.543 --> 13:14.544
- Yeah?
- Mmm.

13:19.508 --> 13:20.717
What unit were you in?

13:21.843 --> 13:24.596
They had me in motor pool in Kiev,
but then they...

13:24.680 --> 13:27.808
Not this bullshit. In Afghanistan.

13:27.891 --> 13:29.267
Oh. Oh, I am...

13:29.351 --> 13:31.019
I wasn't in Afghanistan.

13:33.981 --> 13:34.982
I'm not in the military.

13:39.152 --> 13:40.153
They're running out of men.

13:52.249 --> 13:53.583
Showers. Food.

13:54.167 --> 13:56.336
Those guys, they dig up the ground.

13:56.920 --> 13:58.338
Those guys, they cut down trees.

13:59.506 --> 14:03.927
Those guys, they evacuate people,
I think, like villagers.

14:05.846 --> 14:06.847
What about them?

14:08.098 --> 14:09.558
I don't know them. Fuck them.

14:12.060 --> 14:13.061
Janek!

14:14.980 --> 14:17.441
- What do you want?
- Give me an egg basket.

14:17.649 --> 14:19.901
- No. I've only got the one...
- Give me the fucking basket!

14:24.072 --> 14:27.659
He's with me. You understand?
Nobody fucks with him.

14:30.620 --> 14:32.247
We make these from lead scrap.

14:32.706 --> 14:34.958
- Put it on under your balls.
- Now?

14:35.375 --> 14:37.794
No, no. You can wait
until the radiation gives you a cunt.

14:38.420 --> 14:39.546
Yes, now.

14:41.715 --> 14:44.259
Over your clothes. Fucking shit.

14:52.893 --> 14:54.728
- You ever go hunting?
- No.

14:56.063 --> 14:58.899
Well, today's your lucky day.

14:59.941 --> 15:04.196
You, me, that ugly Armenian
in the tent, Garo,

15:04.362 --> 15:05.572
we do animal control.

15:06.948 --> 15:08.075
Animal control?

15:08.533 --> 15:11.453
Yeah, they're radioactive,
so they have to go.

15:12.996 --> 15:14.498
But it's not hard.
They're mostly pets.

15:15.373 --> 15:18.085
They're happy to see you.
They run right up to you.

15:18.585 --> 15:19.586
Bang!

15:19.669 --> 15:21.171
You load the bodies on a truck,

15:21.505 --> 15:23.673
dump them in a pit,
bury them in concrete,

15:23.757 --> 15:24.841
and then we drink.

15:25.717 --> 15:27.177
As much vodka as you want,

15:28.303 --> 15:29.387
plus 1,000 rubles.

15:32.099 --> 15:33.266
Let's go get you a gun.

16:42.878 --> 16:43.879
Yes?

16:44.337 --> 16:47.507
I need to see the following documents.
They're listed as "permission only."

16:53.930 --> 16:55.140
I'm working for the Central Committee.

17:08.236 --> 17:09.237
Comrade?

17:47.943 --> 17:49.069
She can have that one.

17:58.036 --> 17:59.079
Thank you, Comrade.

19:38.261 --> 19:40.388
- All clear.
- Bring up the cameras.

19:46.478 --> 19:47.979
- Signal?
- Acceptable.

19:48.063 --> 19:49.689
Running on board diagnostics.

19:50.231 --> 19:51.816
Tell me when
we're ready to move it.

19:52.942 --> 19:55.278
To think that's what we put
on the moon.

19:57.572 --> 19:59.032
Well, not that one.

20:01.076 --> 20:02.535
I know not that one.

20:03.703 --> 20:05.663
This rover was in storage.
They can build two more.

20:06.414 --> 20:08.166
That should cover Nina and Katya.

20:09.751 --> 20:10.877
And Masha?

20:11.378 --> 20:13.088
The Central Committee
have informed me

20:13.296 --> 20:16.091
that they may have found something
that could work up there.

20:16.257 --> 20:18.093
- From the outside.
- American?

20:19.094 --> 20:20.303
Of course not.

20:21.096 --> 20:22.639
It's a German police robot.

20:23.431 --> 20:25.392
But West German,
so, as you can imagine,

20:25.475 --> 20:27.519
that wasn't
an easy conversation to have.

20:28.061 --> 20:31.231
Diagnostics complete.
Ready to engage main power and motor.

20:32.482 --> 20:33.483
Begin.

20:39.656 --> 20:40.657
Can we move it?

20:53.962 --> 20:56.673
Valery, what's that? A smile?

21:15.984 --> 21:18.486
I see your condition
has improved, Comrade Dyatlov.

21:18.570 --> 21:19.779
No. Leave.

21:27.996 --> 21:29.080
I need your help.

21:37.714 --> 21:40.175
Akimov initiated AZ-5.

21:41.342 --> 21:43.678
- When you gave the order...
- Order? What order?

21:45.597 --> 21:48.516
Toptunov called it out,
Akimov pressed it.

21:49.767 --> 21:51.352
It was the only
good decision they made.

21:51.436 --> 21:52.437
Incompetent morons.

21:54.314 --> 21:56.858
Can you confirm
that the reactor exploded

21:56.941 --> 21:58.693
after they attempted to shut it down?

21:59.819 --> 22:01.738
How do I even know it exploded, huh?

22:23.218 --> 22:24.385
I found this in the state archive.

22:26.596 --> 22:28.223
Written in 1976.

22:28.973 --> 22:30.141
It's about the operation

22:30.225 --> 22:32.852
of RBMK reactors
under extreme conditions.

22:32.936 --> 22:33.937
So?

22:34.395 --> 22:36.439
The names of the authors
have been redacted,

22:36.898 --> 22:38.566
and two pages have been removed.

22:39.776 --> 22:42.612
Well, the State must protect
its secrets, Comrade.

22:43.238 --> 22:44.781
Do you dare suggest otherwise?

22:46.407 --> 22:47.742
They made a mistake.

22:50.119 --> 22:52.455
They didn't redact
the table of contents.

23:03.550 --> 23:05.176
The missing pages apparently refer

23:05.260 --> 23:08.805
to a positive void coefficient
and AZ-5.

23:10.056 --> 23:11.307
Does that mean anything to you?

23:11.391 --> 23:14.018
What are you after here?
Why are you asking me this?

23:14.102 --> 23:16.312
You worked with this reactor.
You know it better than I do.

23:16.396 --> 23:18.356
So everything's my fault, then?

23:19.524 --> 23:20.608
Is that what this is?

23:20.692 --> 23:23.695
I'm not here to blame you.
I'm here to find out what happened.

23:24.862 --> 23:26.155
And whether you realize it or not,

23:26.239 --> 23:28.324
I'm your best chance
to avoid a bullet.

23:31.119 --> 23:32.495
Can you help me or not?

23:41.963 --> 23:43.756
I have no idea
what would have gone here.

23:43.840 --> 23:46.759
Void coefficients
have nothing to do with AZ-5.

23:47.802 --> 23:49.137
There. Now you can go.

23:49.971 --> 23:52.140
- You're not even curious?
- What for?

23:54.100 --> 23:56.519
You think the right question
will get you the truth?

23:58.313 --> 23:59.689
There's no truth.

24:00.732 --> 24:03.526
Ask the bosses whatever you want
and you'll get the lie.

24:05.028 --> 24:06.738
And I will get the bullet.

25:39.914 --> 25:41.332
I only have two rules.

25:41.916 --> 25:42.917
One.

25:43.876 --> 25:46.337
Don't point this gun at me.
That's easy, right?

25:47.046 --> 25:48.673
You can point it
at this piece of shit.

25:48.756 --> 25:50.425
I don't give a fuck. Never me.

25:51.884 --> 25:52.885
Two.

25:53.261 --> 25:56.139
If you hit an animal
and it doesn't die,

25:56.222 --> 25:57.932
keep shooting until it does.

25:59.267 --> 26:00.601
Don't let them suffer,

26:02.019 --> 26:04.021
or I'll kill you. Understand?

26:05.398 --> 26:06.399
I mean it.

26:07.942 --> 26:09.152
I've killed a lot of people.

26:14.907 --> 26:17.160
Good. Then we're ready.

26:56.949 --> 26:59.952
Once we start, they'll run inside
where they feel safe.

27:01.078 --> 27:02.455
So we go door to door.

27:03.623 --> 27:04.624
Okay?

27:05.249 --> 27:06.250
Good.

27:56.759 --> 27:57.760
Hey!

27:58.427 --> 28:00.721
Do your job. Door to door.

28:54.817 --> 28:56.777
Go. Go.

28:56.903 --> 28:58.863
Go away. Go!

29:55.294 --> 29:56.754
Don't let them suffer.

29:57.380 --> 29:58.547
Sorry. Sorry.

30:01.676 --> 30:03.135
You're dragging that to the truck.

30:40.798 --> 30:41.882
You gonna eat?

30:52.852 --> 30:53.853
Drink.

30:57.898 --> 30:58.899
Again.

31:11.328 --> 31:12.329
Look...

31:15.124 --> 31:17.293
This happens to everyone
their first time.

31:18.419 --> 31:20.129
Normally when you kill a man.

31:22.214 --> 31:23.674
But for you, a dog.

31:24.133 --> 31:26.218
So what? There's no shame in it.

31:28.429 --> 31:30.347
You remember your first time, Garo?

31:31.348 --> 31:34.310
My first time, Afghanistan.

31:36.812 --> 31:38.564
We were moving through a house,

31:39.523 --> 31:42.693
and suddenly a man was there
and I shot him in the stomach.

31:44.987 --> 31:46.864
Yeah, that's a real war story.

31:48.365 --> 31:51.160
There are never any good stories
like in the movies. They're shit.

31:52.912 --> 31:56.207
A man was there, boom, stomach.

31:58.834 --> 32:00.878
I was so scared,
I didn't pull the trigger again

32:00.961 --> 32:02.379
for the rest of the day.

32:04.673 --> 32:07.259
I thought, "Well, that's it, Bacho.

32:08.969 --> 32:10.554
"You put a bullet in someone.

32:11.305 --> 32:13.015
"You're not you anymore.

32:13.682 --> 32:15.101
"You'll never be you again."

32:18.104 --> 32:21.440
But then you wake up the next morning,
and you're still you.

32:22.942 --> 32:24.110
And you realize

32:25.736 --> 32:27.196
that was you all along.

32:28.405 --> 32:29.865
You just didn't know.

32:40.584 --> 32:43.003
"The happiness of all mankind."

32:46.757 --> 32:47.758
What?

32:49.593 --> 32:52.304
"Our goal is the happiness
of all mankind."

33:00.146 --> 33:01.147
Yeah.

33:06.193 --> 33:07.236
I'm happy.

33:07.945 --> 33:09.196
I'm happy every day.

33:11.615 --> 33:12.616
All right.

33:13.993 --> 33:15.077
Back to work.

33:16.328 --> 33:17.329
Come on.

34:36.158 --> 34:37.243
It's here.

35:06.605 --> 35:07.606
All right.

35:09.817 --> 35:11.694
Get over. Right, hang on.

35:14.321 --> 35:15.864
Easy now. Careful.

35:16.865 --> 35:17.866
Hold it!

35:26.417 --> 35:27.418
Joker.

35:29.128 --> 35:31.505
It's what the Germans
named it. "Joker."

35:31.755 --> 35:32.923
Is it ready?

35:33.590 --> 35:34.591
It's ready.

36:22.139 --> 36:23.140
Good signal.

36:24.600 --> 36:25.601
Cameras.

36:27.102 --> 36:28.103
Motors.

36:30.481 --> 36:32.608
Motors, good. Signals, good.

36:33.734 --> 36:35.736
All right, let's take this easy.

36:36.320 --> 36:38.530
Forward one meter, reverse one meter.

36:40.824 --> 36:41.825
Forward one.

36:46.121 --> 36:47.414
Germans.

36:48.999 --> 36:50.125
Reverse one.

37:03.347 --> 37:04.348
Did you lose the signal?

37:10.396 --> 37:11.855
It's not the signal. It's the vehicle.

37:13.774 --> 37:14.858
It's dead.

37:21.365 --> 37:22.366
Shit.

37:27.371 --> 37:29.164
Of course, I know they're listening!

37:29.248 --> 37:31.375
I want them to hear!
I want them to hear it all!

37:31.834 --> 37:33.127
Do you know what we're doing here?

37:33.919 --> 37:35.963
Tell those idiots what they have done!

37:38.048 --> 37:39.716
I don't give a fuck!

37:41.552 --> 37:43.846
Tell them! Go tell them! Ryzhkov!

37:43.929 --> 37:45.139
Go tell them he's a joke!

37:45.222 --> 37:47.182
Tell fucking Gorbachev!

37:47.266 --> 37:48.267
Tell them!

38:11.748 --> 38:13.417
The official position of the State

38:14.418 --> 38:18.589
is that a global nuclear catastrophe
is not possible in the Soviet Union.

38:19.590 --> 38:20.591
They told the Germans

38:20.674 --> 38:25.304
that the highest detected level
of radiation was 2,000 roentgen.

38:27.264 --> 38:28.849
They gave them the propaganda number.

38:31.435 --> 38:33.395
That robot was never going to work.

38:38.066 --> 38:39.359
We need a new phone.

39:21.235 --> 39:22.778
What if we don't clear it?

39:23.362 --> 39:24.613
We have to clear it.

39:26.573 --> 39:29.326
If we don't clear the roof,
we can't build a cover over it.

39:31.662 --> 39:34.289
If we can't cover it,
that's 12,000 roentgen.

39:35.207 --> 39:38.627
Nearly twice the radiation
from the Hiroshima bomb.

39:39.628 --> 39:42.422
- Every hour, hour after hour...
- I know, I know, I know.

39:43.257 --> 39:44.550
What about lead?

39:46.343 --> 39:47.678
We could... I don't know.

39:47.761 --> 39:51.014
We could melt it and pour it
from above, like a coating.

39:51.098 --> 39:52.558
First of all, we've already used

39:52.641 --> 39:54.101
most of the lead we had...

39:54.184 --> 39:56.270
There's lead sheeting
around the instruments

39:56.353 --> 39:58.146
in the other reactor buildings.

39:58.355 --> 40:00.899
The soldiers are stripping it
for their armor.

40:00.983 --> 40:02.150
Are you serious?

40:05.279 --> 40:09.575
Even if, we're still talking
about boiling metal in a helicopter.

40:09.866 --> 40:12.035
And it's lead, Boris.
It'll weigh a ton.

40:14.788 --> 40:18.000
What if we shoot the graphite
into the hole?

40:18.584 --> 40:20.961
We've got high-caliber bullets,
exploding bullets.

40:21.044 --> 40:23.130
They wouldn't just ricochet,
they'd push...

40:23.213 --> 40:27.342
You wanna shoot exploding bullets
at an exposed nuclear reactor?

40:27.426 --> 40:29.011
- Well...
- No, no.

40:29.803 --> 40:31.471
Let's go light that roof back on fire.

40:31.763 --> 40:34.057
It was so easy
to put out the first time.

40:36.310 --> 40:37.853
What are we talking about here?

40:39.938 --> 40:41.481
We need another robot.

40:42.983 --> 40:45.277
One that can withstand the radiation.

40:45.944 --> 40:47.904
I've asked. There is nothing.

40:49.406 --> 40:50.616
The Americans?

40:51.450 --> 40:53.285
If the Americans had
that kind of technology,

40:53.368 --> 40:54.953
do you really think
they'd give it to us?

40:55.037 --> 40:56.038
And even if they would,

40:56.121 --> 40:57.581
the Central Committee
would never stoop to ask.

40:57.956 --> 40:59.291
You know it, I know it.

41:00.917 --> 41:02.127
There are no robots.

41:09.259 --> 41:10.344
Biorobots.

41:11.678 --> 41:12.679
What was that?

41:17.851 --> 41:21.021
We use biorobots.

41:24.191 --> 41:25.192
Men.

42:54.072 --> 42:55.323
A lot today.

43:00.620 --> 43:01.997
Where do they get their food?

43:05.041 --> 43:06.209
They eat the chickens.

43:07.878 --> 43:09.212
Then they eat each other.

43:20.098 --> 43:21.266
Door to door.

44:33.713 --> 44:34.714
Pavel?

44:40.136 --> 44:41.137
Pavel!

44:50.272 --> 44:52.732
You don't hear me? I'm talking to you.

44:55.318 --> 44:56.319
Fuck.

45:01.825 --> 45:02.826
Just go outside.

45:09.916 --> 45:10.917
Go.

48:04.883 --> 48:06.092
Comrade soldiers,

48:06.634 --> 48:09.095
the Soviet people have had
enough of this accident.

48:09.637 --> 48:11.056
They want us to clean it up,

48:11.139 --> 48:13.558
and we have entrusted you
with this serious task.

48:14.225 --> 48:15.685
Because of the nature
of the working area,

48:16.227 --> 48:19.606
you will each have no more
than 90 seconds to solve this problem.

48:20.273 --> 48:23.026
Listen carefully
to each of my instructions,

48:23.109 --> 48:25.695
and do exactly as you have been told.

48:25.779 --> 48:29.741
This is for your own safety
and the safety of your comrades.

48:30.492 --> 48:32.368
You will enter Reactor Building Three.

48:32.869 --> 48:36.498
Climb the stairs, but do not
immediately proceed to the roof

48:36.581 --> 48:38.833
When you get to the top, wait inside,

48:38.917 --> 48:41.252
behind the entrance to the roof
and catch your breath.

48:41.795 --> 48:44.047
You will need it for what comes next.

48:44.464 --> 48:47.634
This is the working area.
We must clear the graphite.

48:47.717 --> 48:48.927
Some of it is in blocks,

48:49.010 --> 48:51.137
weighing approximately
40 to 50 kilograms.

48:51.221 --> 48:53.389
They all must be thrown
over the edge here.

48:53.807 --> 48:57.143
Watch your comrades
moving fast from this opening,

48:57.227 --> 49:00.814
then turning to the left,
and entering the workspace here.

49:01.189 --> 49:02.774
Take care not to stumble.

49:03.441 --> 49:05.443
There's a hole in the roof
Take care not to fall.

49:06.861 --> 49:10.198
You will need to move quickly,
and you will need to move carefully.

49:11.449 --> 49:13.827
Do you understand your mission
as I have described it?

49:13.910 --> 49:15.578
Yes, Comrade General.

49:15.995 --> 49:19.040
These are the most important
90 seconds of your lives.

49:19.499 --> 49:22.710
Commit your task to memory,
then do your job.

50:05.879 --> 50:08.756
It's time to go.
After 90 seconds, I will ring a bell.

50:08.923 --> 50:11.634
When you hear it, return immediately,
drop your shovels in the bin,

50:12.135 --> 50:14.512
and proceed down the hallway
for decontamination.

50:15.096 --> 50:18.266
Above all, while on the roof,
throw your debris over the rail.

50:18.349 --> 50:19.976
Do not look over the rail.
Is that clear?

50:21.352 --> 50:25.315
Very well. On my mark. Ready. Go.

52:04.831 --> 52:06.666
Whoa!

52:38.323 --> 52:39.324
Comrade soldier.

52:41.200 --> 52:42.201
You're done.

52:54.672 --> 52:55.757
Time to go.

53:08.895 --> 53:10.480
Oi! Your glove!

53:31.250 --> 53:32.418
Mommy! Mommy!

54:37.275 --> 54:38.443
Sorry for all this.

54:39.694 --> 54:42.071
But we needed to speak to you
somewhere without...

54:43.823 --> 54:45.783
They're going to put
Dyatlov on trial,

54:46.701 --> 54:48.494
and Bryukhanov and Fomin.

54:48.828 --> 54:52.415
We're going to be asked
to give expert testimony,

54:52.623 --> 54:53.708
all three of us.

54:54.292 --> 54:55.293
But that's...

54:55.626 --> 54:56.669
Before that happens...

54:57.044 --> 55:00.381
The Central Committee
is sending Legasov to Vienna.

55:00.465 --> 55:02.467
It's the headquarters
of the International Atomic...

55:02.550 --> 55:05.553
Atomic Energy Agency.
Yeah, I know what's in Vienna.

55:07.680 --> 55:09.348
What are they asking you to do?

55:10.141 --> 55:11.601
Tell the world what happened.

55:17.148 --> 55:18.608
Well, then you'd better
know what happened.

55:19.484 --> 55:22.570
I've constructed a timeline,
minute by minute.

55:23.571 --> 55:25.406
Second by second in some places.

55:26.491 --> 55:29.660
Every decision, every button push,
every turn of a switch.

55:30.411 --> 55:32.413
And? Are they guilty?

55:33.289 --> 55:34.290
Yes.

55:35.249 --> 55:38.794
Of gross incompetence,
violation of safety regulations,

55:38.878 --> 55:40.505
recklessness beyond belief.

55:41.172 --> 55:43.758
But the explosion? I'm not sure.

55:43.966 --> 55:45.426
What do you mean, you're not sure?

55:46.886 --> 55:48.513
I've analyzed the data.

55:49.180 --> 55:50.932
Toptunov was telling the truth.

55:51.599 --> 55:54.435
They shut the reactor down,
and then it exploded.

55:56.187 --> 55:58.648
I think
this article may have the answer,

55:59.649 --> 56:02.068
but two pages have been removed.

56:08.574 --> 56:09.992
You've seen this before.

56:10.660 --> 56:13.246
Please, believe me when I tell you

56:13.454 --> 56:15.831
that I had no idea
it could cause an explosion.

56:15.915 --> 56:18.918
- None of us knew.
- None of you knew what?

56:20.294 --> 56:23.172
In 1975, at an RBMK reactor
in Leningrad,

56:23.714 --> 56:27.510
a fuel channel ruptured.
The operators pressed AZ-5,

56:27.593 --> 56:30.096
but instead of the power
going down immediately,

56:30.471 --> 56:33.140
for a brief moment, it went up.

56:33.849 --> 56:35.142
How is that possible?

56:35.226 --> 56:38.688
Well, this was the very question posed
by a colleague of mine named Volkov.

56:38.771 --> 56:40.273
He's the one who wrote this article.

56:40.940 --> 56:42.858
When an RBMK reactor runs
at low power,

56:42.942 --> 56:44.569
it's notoriously unstable.

56:44.735 --> 56:46.737
Prone to swings in reactivity.

56:47.947 --> 56:50.116
Under normal circumstances,
the control rods

56:50.199 --> 56:52.702
- can compensate for that.
- Under normal circumstances.

56:52.785 --> 56:56.205
The Chernobyl staff stalled
the reactor during the test.

56:56.622 --> 56:58.291
They pulled
almost all the control rods out

56:58.374 --> 56:59.417
to bring the power back up.

56:59.500 --> 57:01.919
This is what Volkov learned
from Leningrad.

57:02.295 --> 57:05.131
If the boron control rods
are completely withdrawn

57:05.214 --> 57:07.633
from the reactor,
when they're put back in,

57:07.717 --> 57:11.012
the first thing
that enters the core isn't boron.

57:11.804 --> 57:13.055
It's graphite.

57:16.517 --> 57:20.688
The control rods have graphite tips
that displace water and steam.

57:21.314 --> 57:25.359
So the reactivity doesn't go down.
It goes up dramatically.

57:26.861 --> 57:29.196
Why on earth
would they press that button?

57:29.739 --> 57:30.906
They didn't know.

57:33.242 --> 57:34.869
Volkov warned the Kremlin,

57:35.870 --> 57:36.954
10 years ago.

57:39.206 --> 57:42.752
But there could be no doubt
about the supremacy

57:42.835 --> 57:44.920
of the Soviet nuclear industry.

57:45.630 --> 57:46.631
Oh.

57:46.964 --> 57:50.176
The KGB classified it
as a state secret.

57:52.887 --> 57:54.263
When I saw
the reactor blown open,

57:54.347 --> 57:57.183
I still didn't think
it could be this flaw in AZ-5.

57:58.017 --> 58:01.187
Because the flaw will not lead
to an explosion

58:01.437 --> 58:06.067
unless the operators have pushed
the reactor to the edge of disaster.

58:06.400 --> 58:08.486
- So it is their fault?
- Yes.

58:09.236 --> 58:10.655
But not only their fault.

58:12.615 --> 58:13.616
No.

58:15.368 --> 58:17.370
Is that
what you're going to say in Vienna?

58:21.374 --> 58:23.626
You can't possibly be that naive.

58:24.460 --> 58:30.174
There are 16 RBMK reactors
running in the Soviet Union right now.

58:30.257 --> 58:31.842
We have to fix them.

58:32.343 --> 58:35.137
The only way to do that
is to go public,

58:35.304 --> 58:37.264
force the Central Committee
to take action.

58:37.348 --> 58:40.267
What you're proposing
is that Legasov humiliate a nation

58:40.351 --> 58:43.270
that is obsessed
with not being humiliated.

58:43.396 --> 58:45.106
We can make a deal with the KGB.

58:45.981 --> 58:48.150
You'll leave this information out
in Vienna,

58:48.317 --> 58:51.112
and they quietly
let us fix the remaining reactors.

58:51.195 --> 58:54.782
A deal with the KGB? And I'm naive.

58:56.826 --> 59:00.246
They'll go after your family,
they'll go after your friends.

59:00.329 --> 59:02.873
You have a chance
to talk to the world, Valery.

59:03.165 --> 59:05.042
If that chance was mine...

59:05.126 --> 59:06.377
But it isn't, is it?

59:08.087 --> 59:10.464
I've known braver souls
than you, Khomyuk.

59:11.257 --> 59:13.259
Men who had their moment
and did nothing.

59:13.509 --> 59:16.595
Because when it's your life
and the lives of everyone you love,

59:17.763 --> 59:19.807
your moral conviction
doesn't mean anything.

59:20.266 --> 59:21.392
It leaves you.

59:22.768 --> 59:26.480
And all you want at that moment
is not to be shot.

59:31.235 --> 59:33.529
Do you know the name Vasily Ignatenko?

59:34.447 --> 59:35.448
No.

59:36.365 --> 59:37.616
He was a fireman.

59:39.368 --> 59:41.537
He died two weeks after the accident.

59:42.621 --> 59:44.206
I've been looking in on his widow.

59:45.458 --> 59:47.793
She gave birth. A girl.

59:48.836 --> 59:50.588
The baby lived for four hours.

59:52.381 --> 59:54.049
They said the radiation
would have killed the mother,

59:54.133 --> 59:55.968
but the baby absorbed it instead.

59:56.886 --> 59:57.887
Her baby.

01:00:00.139 --> 01:00:01.265
We live in a country

01:00:01.599 --> 01:00:04.018
where children have to die
to save their mothers.

01:00:05.478 --> 01:00:06.520
To hell with your deal.

01:00:09.648 --> 01:00:11.025
And to hell with our lives.

01:00:13.694 --> 01:00:15.362
Someone has to start
telling the truth.

01:00:30.169 --> 01:00:31.921
Congratulations, comrades.

01:00:32.588 --> 01:00:36.008
You are the last of 3,828 men.

01:00:36.509 --> 01:00:38.844
You have performed
your duties perfectly.

01:00:38.928 --> 01:00:41.180
I wish you good health and long life.

01:00:41.430 --> 01:00:44.308
All of you are awarded
a bonus of 800 rubles.

01:00:44.475 --> 01:00:46.060
- Thank you.
- I serve the Soviet Union.

01:00:46.143 --> 01:00:47.978
- Thank you.
- I serve the Soviet Union.

01:00:48.062 --> 01:00:49.814
- Thank you.
- I serve the Soviet Union.

01:00:49.897 --> 01:00:51.524
- Thank you.
- I serve the Soviet Union.

01:00:51.607 --> 01:00:53.567
- Thank you.
- I serve the Soviet Union.

01:00:53.651 --> 01:00:55.319
- Thank you.
- I serve the Soviet Union.

01:00:55.402 --> 01:00:56.946
- Thank you.
- I serve the Soviet Union.

01:00:57.029 --> 01:00:58.364
- Thank you.
- I serve the Soviet Union.

01:00:58.447 --> 01:01:00.407
- Thank you.
- I serve the Soviet Union.
